WEBVTT

00:08.740 --> 00:16.040
Note: Expression meaning a polar shift in mindset.

00:08.740 --> 00:12.580
This is what you'd call <i>kopeten</i>, right?

00:13.030 --> 00:15.500
"Copernican Revolution."

00:16.370 --> 00:18.250
That's why, I...

00:23.670 --> 00:29.590
Note: Kirameki, the name of Fumika's father, means glitter.

00:33.430 --> 00:33.680
The true forms

00:35.270 --> 00:35.520
Of the things that I gazed at

00:37.140 --> 00:37.390
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

00:38.270 --> 00:41.150
Shigofumi

00:40.850 --> 00:41.100
Again today, time

00:42.690 --> 00:42.940
Will only construct a loneliness

00:44.480 --> 00:44.730
That seems to be torn apart, right?

00:44.730 --> 00:48.240
That seems to be torn apart, right?

00:52.160 --> 00:55.620
There are people who can't forget about

00:55.830 --> 00:59.210
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

00:59.460 --> 01:02.920
Nevertheless, recollections

01:03.210 --> 01:06.630
Visit from the future

01:06.880 --> 01:14.300
Words that turn into sighs

01:14.300 --> 01:17.890
Are the emerging wings of the soul

01:17.970 --> 01:21.440
Will I flutter apart?

01:21.690 --> 01:25.230
Growing confused and disordered

01:25.360 --> 01:27.690
I want to carve

01:27.690 --> 01:31.150
These letters to you

01:32.700 --> 01:34.530
Pieces of the truth

01:34.530 --> 01:36.330
Of things that I want to tell you-

01:36.410 --> 01:39.910
I can't even send them well to you

01:40.160 --> 01:43.630
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

01:43.830 --> 01:47.210
Then can they spill into your heart?

01:47.500 --> 01:50.420
Even if the one word left behind

01:50.760 --> 01:53.470
To us who live

01:53.470 --> 01:58.810
Is to be goodbye

02:06.730 --> 02:09.070
Kagurazaka-san is getting married?

02:09.070 --> 02:11.440
Yeah, I heard to someone from the sales department.

02:11.740 --> 02:13.070
How surprising.

02:13.360 --> 02:17.030
The last time I met her, she said
that she wasn't going out with anyone.

02:22.040 --> 02:24.000
You shouldn't believe her, Haruno.

02:24.000 --> 02:25.750
She was obviously hiding it.

02:26.040 --> 02:28.540
I see! So I got tricked.

02:28.540 --> 02:30.250
This is no laughing matter.

02:30.250 --> 02:32.220
You don't have a boyfriend, right?

02:32.670 --> 02:34.720
You don't think I'm hiding that fact?

02:34.720 --> 02:36.680
You're bad at telling lies though.

02:36.680 --> 02:38.140
Am I that easy to read?

02:38.140 --> 02:41.180
Don't you wish to get married?
Maybe a formal marriage interview?

02:44.060 --> 02:49.020
Well, you see. Right now, I'm having more fun reading novels.

02:49.020 --> 02:53.650
Even though you're an editor, all they
make you do is print stuff and serve tea.

02:53.650 --> 02:55.030
You're no different from an office lady.

02:55.030 --> 02:58.570
I can't help it. I'm only in my third year.

03:02.330 --> 03:03.540
Kasai-san.

03:03.540 --> 03:05.960
Can you make twelve copies of this?

03:05.960 --> 03:06.540
Sure.

03:08.880 --> 03:11.920
It's already my third year, isn't it?

03:11.920 --> 03:13.010
Kasai-san!

03:13.010 --> 03:13.760
Yes?

03:14.880 --> 03:18.390
Kasai-san, you like Mikawa Kirameki, don't you?

03:18.390 --> 03:20.640
Yes, I'm a big fan of his.

03:20.640 --> 03:23.020
I even wrote him a fan letter in middle school.

03:23.020 --> 03:25.230
I see. So, it's an "okay", right?

03:25.940 --> 03:27.400
What is this regarding?

03:27.730 --> 03:32.280
You'll be in charge of the Mikawa
Kirameki assignment starting today.

03:34.030 --> 03:37.030
We've got no choice. Let's do it then, Yaji-san?

03:37.030 --> 03:38.160
Agreed, Kita-san.

03:38.740 --> 03:41.280
<i>You bastards looking for a fight?!</i>

03:42.790 --> 03:44.120
I'm home.

03:44.950 --> 03:46.500
Welcome home.

03:45.660 --> 03:46.830
<i>Careful!</i>

03:46.500 --> 03:48.000
What are you watching?

03:46.830 --> 03:48.880
<i>I'm really pissed off today!</i>

03:49.210 --> 03:51.420
Ah, "Yaji and Kita", huh?

03:51.420 --> 03:56.470
Male companions back in this movie's era were tough and
rebellious. They had no intention of negotiating with anyone.

03:56.470 --> 03:58.890
It feels very genuine.

03:59.300 --> 04:01.140
What is it?

04:02.680 --> 04:04.470
By the way, elder sister...

04:04.470 --> 04:06.850
What might it be, my younger sister?

04:06.850 --> 04:12.190
Actually, there is a book that I wish
to borrow at this present moment.

04:13.690 --> 04:15.990
Have you found a boy that you like?

04:16.690 --> 04:18.280
What's the boy like this time?

04:18.820 --> 04:19.700
How did you know?

04:20.570 --> 04:25.870
Because, you only read books when you've
found a boy that you like, right, Na-chan?

04:25.870 --> 04:27.960
You want to read the same book as him, right?

04:27.960 --> 04:29.250
You're getting the wrong idea.

04:29.250 --> 04:30.290
Right, right.

04:30.630 --> 04:35.670
You always go for the brainy boys, don't you?

04:38.550 --> 04:42.640
Because, I like boys who have opposite traits of me.

04:43.300 --> 04:45.010
So, which book?

04:45.520 --> 04:47.140
Mikawa Kirameki.

04:47.140 --> 04:47.890
Wha-?

04:47.890 --> 04:49.980
You don't have to watch what you say though.

04:50.310 --> 04:53.480
It's true that I was in the same school as his daughter.

04:53.480 --> 04:55.900
But, that was four years ago.

04:56.570 --> 04:57.740
I see.

05:00.860 --> 05:05.240
Hey, Na-chan. I'm now in charge
of the Mikawa Kirameki assignment.

05:05.240 --> 05:07.040
What? Really?

05:07.040 --> 05:08.620
What a coincidence.

05:08.620 --> 05:09.750
Good for you!

05:09.750 --> 05:12.210
Is this the first time you've been
in charge of an author assignment?

05:12.210 --> 05:16.130
Yeah. I've always been a fan of his, so I'm really nervous.

05:16.750 --> 05:18.710
Nojima Kaname

05:18.710 --> 05:19.920
Kana...

05:19.920 --> 05:22.220
Nojima Kaname?

05:25.560 --> 05:27.100
Hello, Kaname-kun?

05:27.100 --> 05:28.980
Yeah, Natsuka speaking.

05:30.390 --> 05:31.480
Huh? You want to talk?

05:31.480 --> 05:32.690
How nice.

05:47.030 --> 05:49.580
Sheesh, you sound so happy.

05:49.580 --> 05:52.620
Because there is sorrow, happiness becomes more apparent.

05:52.620 --> 05:54.460
What sorrow are you talking about?

05:54.460 --> 05:56.790
So says the source of my sorrow, huh?

05:57.090 --> 06:00.170
What the heck is that? Even I...

06:01.630 --> 06:04.140
Hey, Fumika!

06:06.390 --> 06:08.390
Sheesh. She's ignoring me.

06:11.100 --> 06:13.020
Mikawa Kirameki.

06:13.020 --> 06:15.480
So, he's the recipient for our next assignment?

06:15.940 --> 06:16.690
Yes.

06:17.020 --> 06:21.740
Who's he? It's rare to see such a reaction from you.

06:21.740 --> 06:24.490
Someone you crossed paths with while you were alive?

06:27.370 --> 06:29.950
The person I shot when I was still alive.

06:36.830 --> 06:38.340
Drinks, check.

06:38.840 --> 06:40.380
Cakes, check.

06:41.710 --> 06:43.840
Father and Sis are at work.

06:43.840 --> 06:45.760
And Mum is out.

06:46.090 --> 06:47.720
Stay calm, Natsuka.

06:47.720 --> 06:49.560
After all, it's regarding Fumika.

06:49.560 --> 06:51.720
If it weren't, then he and I...

06:52.730 --> 06:53.600
A thief?!

06:55.690 --> 06:58.480
Sis, aren't you supposed to be at work?

06:59.020 --> 07:00.440
I overslept...

07:01.530 --> 07:03.690
My alarm clock stopped.

07:03.820 --> 07:07.110
You mean <i>you</i> stopped it, right? Honestly!

07:07.910 --> 07:12.240
It's okay. I'll make it in time if
I head directly to Kirameki-sensei's place.

07:12.700 --> 07:14.160
I'm off.

07:16.250 --> 07:17.750
Kaname-kun!

07:17.750 --> 07:20.210
Guess I arrived a little early.

07:20.210 --> 07:23.590
Oh, my! What an intelligent, cultured looking young man.

07:23.590 --> 07:24.260
Eh?

07:24.260 --> 07:27.220
Please take care of our Natsuka.

07:27.220 --> 07:28.640
Oh, of course.

07:29.600 --> 07:31.850
I'll get upset if you make her cry.

07:32.310 --> 07:33.470
Sis!

07:34.140 --> 07:35.890
I'm off.

07:37.520 --> 07:39.110
Sorry about that.

07:39.440 --> 07:41.980
Come in. For now...

07:41.980 --> 07:43.610
O-Okay...

07:46.320 --> 07:47.490
The hospital?

07:47.490 --> 07:50.320
Has your father been admitted?

07:50.320 --> 07:52.120
No, he's at home.

07:52.120 --> 07:53.370
Then why are you here?

07:53.700 --> 07:55.500
Just a detour.

07:56.000 --> 07:58.040
But, it's an important one.

08:05.420 --> 08:06.220
Well...

08:06.220 --> 08:07.050
Yes?

08:07.340 --> 08:10.430
Something came up and I needed a favour.

08:10.430 --> 08:12.430
It's regarding Mikawa however.

08:13.260 --> 08:15.770
Okay, I understand.

08:15.770 --> 08:16.640
What is it?

08:16.640 --> 08:18.020
Nothing.

08:18.020 --> 08:20.980
Didn't you say that Fumika rejected you?

08:21.560 --> 08:25.940
I wasn't exactly planning on confessing to her again.

08:26.440 --> 08:28.320
I just want to know.

08:29.360 --> 08:31.620
I met Mikawa.

08:32.160 --> 08:34.660
But, that should not have been possible.

08:35.620 --> 08:37.160
What are you saying?

08:37.160 --> 08:39.580
Because, Mikawa has...

08:41.330 --> 08:43.710
been unconscious all this time?

08:43.710 --> 08:46.920
Yes, ever since four years ago.

08:47.550 --> 08:50.050
But, I met her. Probably.

08:50.050 --> 08:52.720
Just a coincidental resemblance maybe?

08:53.140 --> 08:54.890
Who is she?

08:54.890 --> 08:57.350
Why does she look exactly like you, Fumika?

08:57.850 --> 09:00.350
Fumi-chan, a fragment of me.

09:00.730 --> 09:02.310
Fragment?

09:02.690 --> 09:06.610
Did she have anything to do with your father's shooting?

09:07.530 --> 09:09.070
I want to ascertain it.

09:09.070 --> 09:11.530
Why did Mikawa shoot her father?

09:11.530 --> 09:13.280
Why won't she wake up?

09:14.160 --> 09:15.240
That's why...

09:18.250 --> 09:18.500
Incoming Call

09:18.500 --> 09:20.960
Incoming

09:18.500 --> 09:20.960
Haruno

09:19.290 --> 09:20.960
<i>Did I catch you at a bad time?</i>

09:21.290 --> 09:23.500
<i>Pardon me if I interrupted the part where you were kissing.</i>

09:23.500 --> 09:25.040
W-We're not doing anything like that!

09:25.340 --> 09:26.670
How boring.

09:26.670 --> 09:27.630
<i>I'm going to hang up.</i>

09:27.630 --> 09:30.760
I forgot to bring the map to Kirameki-sensei's house...

09:31.180 --> 09:33.260
<i>Can you send it to my cellphone?</i>

09:33.260 --> 09:35.390
<i>There's a scanner in my room.</i>

09:35.390 --> 09:38.770
What? I don't know how to use a scanner.

09:40.850 --> 09:42.100
Here it comes!

09:43.650 --> 09:45.310
Thank you, Na-chan.

09:47.860 --> 09:50.030
Thank you. You were a great help.

09:50.030 --> 09:53.450
Your sister is in charge of the Mikawa Kirameki assignment?

09:53.450 --> 09:55.870
Yeah, it was a recent development.

09:55.870 --> 09:56.450
I see.

10:02.040 --> 10:02.830
What are you doing?

10:02.830 --> 10:04.500
It's the map we sent earlier.

10:04.500 --> 10:07.840
I'd like to ascertain Mikawa's situation
by directly meeting with Mikawa Kirameki.

10:08.590 --> 10:09.510
But...

10:09.510 --> 10:14.970
Only Mikawa Kirameki would know about
the mystery behind why she won't wake up.

10:15.470 --> 10:15.590
Mikawa Kirameki's House is

10:15.470 --> 10:15.590
Inside

10:15.470 --> 10:15.590
the

10:15.470 --> 10:15.590
Forest

10:15.470 --> 10:15.510
Never Ending
Silver Road

10:15.470 --> 10:15.510
Stone
Bridge

10:15.470 --> 10:15.510
Buddhist
Statue

10:15.470 --> 10:15.550
Some
Road

10:15.470 --> 10:15.590
Bus Stop

10:15.470 --> 10:15.590
Kamome City

10:15.590 --> 10:15.720
Mikawa Kirameki's House is

10:20.600 --> 10:22.020
So, it's over there?

10:51.670 --> 10:55.800
The never ending silver road.

10:56.470 --> 11:00.850
Please, Ochida-kun. Let me see Mikawa Kirameki's new book.

11:00.850 --> 11:03.350
He hasn't released anything in four years, has he?

11:03.350 --> 11:05.690
Don't make it sound like it doesn't involve us.

11:05.690 --> 11:08.110
It would sell over 800,000 copies if he released.

11:08.440 --> 11:10.980
I switched in one of my younger employees to be in charge.

11:10.980 --> 11:12.150
Who?

11:12.150 --> 11:13.570
Kasai Haruno-san.

11:14.360 --> 11:16.910
Oh. Didn't you say that she was useless?

11:16.910 --> 11:18.030
Will it be all right?

11:18.030 --> 11:18.950
I've no idea.

11:18.950 --> 11:20.030
No idea?

11:20.330 --> 11:24.410
Well, since she's useless in the first place,
there'd be no regrets even if she failed the assignment.

11:36.720 --> 11:38.550
Yes, who is it?

11:38.550 --> 11:42.060
Umm, how do you do? I'm...

11:42.470 --> 11:47.440
I'm Kasai Haruno from the first
editing department of Itabashi Publications.

11:47.440 --> 11:49.230
Pleased to meet you.

11:49.230 --> 11:52.320
Yes, I had heard that there was a new person in charge.

11:52.320 --> 11:52.940
Am I right?

11:54.030 --> 11:57.070
I'm Mikawa Kirameki. Pleased to meet you.

11:59.240 --> 12:01.950
I'm going to go see Mikawa Kirameki after this.

12:02.790 --> 12:05.450
But, I wanted to see your face before I go.

12:10.540 --> 12:11.670
Fumi-chan...

12:12.540 --> 12:13.550
Forgive me.

12:14.130 --> 12:16.130
Shigofumi

12:17.220 --> 12:19.220
Shigofumi

12:30.650 --> 12:32.110
They're so pretty.

12:32.110 --> 12:34.530
They're all glass pens, aren't they?

12:34.530 --> 12:39.450
Yes. I can write more beautifully
using those instead of metallic pens.

12:40.320 --> 12:41.410
Come.

12:41.410 --> 12:43.780
Let's talk in the light.

12:43.780 --> 12:44.660
Sure.

12:52.040 --> 12:53.630
Glass is beautiful.

12:53.960 --> 12:55.750
The continuity of glittering time.

12:56.260 --> 12:59.590
It is true bliss being bathed in the light.

13:00.090 --> 13:02.260
Ah, the glitter.

13:03.140 --> 13:06.220
The glitter of the glass.

13:08.180 --> 13:10.690
I hate word processors and ballpoint pens.

13:11.480 --> 13:14.610
They aren't beautiful.

13:16.320 --> 13:18.940
That's right. I brought the manuscript.

13:18.940 --> 13:22.610
I got it from the fair the other day
when it was on display. Here you go.

13:27.660 --> 13:28.410
Be quiet.

13:52.560 --> 13:55.650
That's right. I forgot to prepare the tea.

13:56.190 --> 13:59.320
I have some lovely herbal tea. I'll go get it.

14:03.570 --> 14:03.610
The Glitter Within the Light

14:06.580 --> 14:11.540
I often hear that writers can be strange people, but...

14:14.630 --> 14:15.670
That's not the one.

14:18.750 --> 14:23.970
I think that it was because she thought
that I was a person who didn't read books at all.

14:23.970 --> 14:25.180
What's that supposed to mean?

14:25.550 --> 14:31.770
I think Fumika was sick and tired of
being seen as Mikawa Kirameki's daughter.

14:33.770 --> 14:35.440
All right! All done!

14:35.730 --> 14:39.530
Mikawa Kirameki? A singer?

14:39.530 --> 14:43.650
Sorry, I'm not interested in Enka music.

14:44.490 --> 14:45.410
Did I get it wrong?

14:47.070 --> 14:48.160
Sorry.

14:50.870 --> 14:53.830
Since then, I started talking with Fumika.

14:54.120 --> 14:55.370
I see.

14:56.210 --> 14:58.590
Fumika was a girl of few words.

14:58.590 --> 15:03.260
She was always in the infirmary,
so I don't know much about her.

15:03.260 --> 15:04.630
Just...

15:04.630 --> 15:05.470
Just?

15:06.430 --> 15:09.220
Once, she asked me this question.

15:09.220 --> 15:12.220
She asked what kind of person my father was.

15:16.850 --> 15:18.110
Really?

15:18.110 --> 15:20.070
You think that highly of me?

15:20.070 --> 15:21.440
I'm very surprised.

15:21.440 --> 15:25.450
You didn't even do a small rewrite.
There isn't even a rough draft, is there?

15:22.990 --> 15:24.450
Mikawa

15:22.990 --> 15:24.450
Kirameki

15:25.450 --> 15:27.700
You really are an amazing person.

15:27.990 --> 15:30.870
I spent a lot of time planning the plot.

15:30.870 --> 15:34.500
Can you show me your work area?

15:35.160 --> 15:36.210
Work area?

15:36.500 --> 15:40.380
I was wondering in what kind of place you
work in to produce such a wonderful script.

15:40.380 --> 15:41.300
No, you can't see it!

15:42.630 --> 15:43.800
Forgive me.

15:43.800 --> 15:46.800
My work area is a mess.

15:46.800 --> 15:48.180
It embarrasses me.

15:48.180 --> 15:51.010
Not at all. Me too, I'm sorry for being so impolite.

15:54.180 --> 15:55.270
Rain?

15:55.560 --> 15:57.850
And there was only a ten percent chance.

15:57.850 --> 16:00.440
A sunshower, surely.

16:00.440 --> 16:01.860
Sunshower?

16:02.440 --> 16:03.610
So, it's a sunshower?

16:04.190 --> 16:05.990
Raining even though it's sunny?

16:07.610 --> 16:08.990
A sunshower, eh?

16:11.620 --> 16:13.660
Rain, glitter!

16:16.210 --> 16:21.670
Rain, rain, rain even though it's sunny.

16:24.210 --> 16:26.590
You're going to catch a cold like that.

16:36.640 --> 16:38.190
Come, you too.

16:38.190 --> 16:40.440
It's a sunshower, you know!

16:41.900 --> 16:43.820
There was a film like this too, wasn't there?

16:51.780 --> 16:54.280
Shall we dance?

17:00.080 --> 17:02.080
It's clearing up.

17:02.080 --> 17:04.250
It sure slowed us down terribly.

17:05.960 --> 17:07.550
Now, the problem is...

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Mikawa Kirameki's House is

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Inside

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
the

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Forest

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Never Ending
Silver Road

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Stone Bridge

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Buddhist
Statue

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Some
Road

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Bus Stop

17:09.260 --> 17:09.300
Kamome City

17:09.300 --> 17:09.340
Mikawa Kirameki's House is

17:09.550 --> 17:15.390
figuring out the way to Mikawa Kirameki's
house from these extremely vague directions.

17:25.360 --> 17:27.610
Don't you want to get married?

17:31.820 --> 17:33.030
What's that?

17:33.030 --> 17:35.450
That must be the silver road.

17:35.450 --> 17:37.040
You think so?

17:38.620 --> 17:39.330
Hey.

17:39.870 --> 17:42.920
That's great. Looks like the size fits.

17:42.920 --> 17:45.630
Yes. Thank you very much.

17:46.630 --> 17:49.840
<i>But, whose clothes are these?</i>

17:49.840 --> 17:52.550
<i>His daughter? Or perhaps...</i>

18:02.190 --> 18:03.270
Who might you be?

18:03.270 --> 18:07.110
Umm, wait. Let me guess.

18:11.820 --> 18:13.200
The postman.

18:13.740 --> 18:14.870
I got it right!

18:15.950 --> 18:19.490
Thank you, I'll take it.

18:20.370 --> 18:21.960
Is it fan mail?

18:21.960 --> 18:23.330
That sure brings back memories.

18:23.710 --> 18:26.920
I sent you one a long time ago too.

18:26.920 --> 18:29.090
I was so emotionally moved when you replied.

18:29.420 --> 18:34.760
But, I found out that it was written
by the editor after I joined the company.

18:37.550 --> 18:39.430
What's the matter?

18:40.600 --> 18:44.310
Can I read it?

18:45.310 --> 18:46.730
I'm going to read it.

18:48.520 --> 18:50.730
This handwriting looks like it's written by a middle schooler.

18:51.820 --> 18:54.570
How do you do, Kirameki-sensei?

18:54.570 --> 18:57.450
I'm Njord of Silver.

18:57.990 --> 19:00.620
I've read all your books.

19:00.620 --> 19:02.330
Over and over.

19:02.790 --> 19:04.960
They're beautiful and cruel.

19:04.960 --> 19:06.420
I loved them.

19:07.500 --> 19:10.500
Death is very much like a frozen world.

19:11.050 --> 19:13.760
Nothing lives, no colours.

19:13.760 --> 19:17.140
Conversely, there are no germs and no filth either.

19:18.800 --> 19:21.930
An ultimately clean world.

19:22.640 --> 19:25.350
There is nothing sad about death.

19:25.640 --> 19:27.150
Everything stops.

19:27.520 --> 19:30.020
A pure and beautiful world.

19:31.320 --> 19:33.110
There is nothing to fear.

19:34.610 --> 19:35.740
How lovely.

19:36.320 --> 19:39.240
Up until now, I was scared of the dark world of the dead.

19:39.240 --> 19:41.450
But now, I feel the opposite.

19:42.240 --> 19:46.040
This is what you'd call <i>kopeten</i>, right?

19:46.540 --> 19:48.830
"Copernican Revolution."

19:49.710 --> 19:51.800
That's why, I...

20:01.010 --> 20:02.350
Shigofumi.

20:04.810 --> 20:07.480
A letter from the world of the departed.

20:07.480 --> 20:09.190
That's why it's called a Shigofumi.

20:10.400 --> 20:13.110
Who are you?

20:14.900 --> 20:17.030
I found it!

20:17.820 --> 20:19.320
The holy flame!

20:19.820 --> 20:21.830
A lighter?

20:21.830 --> 20:24.240
Yep. I'm going to burn that letter.

20:26.660 --> 20:29.000
Kaname-kun, are you okay?

20:29.000 --> 20:29.830
Yeah.

20:30.130 --> 20:33.130
Don't do it. It's a letter from a fan.

20:33.130 --> 20:34.250
So?

20:36.090 --> 20:38.130
Terrible handwriting. Over-reliance on others.

20:38.130 --> 20:40.340
Self-deluded. Narcissistic.

20:40.340 --> 20:42.100
An unfashionable envelope.

20:42.100 --> 20:44.470
It's all so filthy.

20:44.470 --> 20:47.140
That's why I'm going to burn it with beautiful flames.

20:47.140 --> 20:50.600
These are sentiments from your reader.

20:50.600 --> 20:53.270
Her feelings may not reach you, but she tried her best...

20:53.270 --> 20:56.030
I can't accept effort as a selling point.

20:57.030 --> 20:58.450
You haven't changed.

20:58.450 --> 20:59.700
Not even a little.

21:00.320 --> 21:05.240
You've never once thought that people
other than yourself have feelings as well.

21:05.240 --> 21:07.290
That's why you lost them.

21:07.290 --> 21:09.830
Mother and your daughter too.

21:10.330 --> 21:11.710
Your daughters.

21:13.000 --> 21:14.210
Fumika?

21:14.750 --> 21:17.050
So, it's you, Fumika?

21:17.050 --> 21:18.260
This is Fumika.

21:18.920 --> 21:20.510
She's my daughter.

21:23.350 --> 21:24.010
Mikawa!

21:26.140 --> 21:30.230
Remember! I shot you with this.

21:30.230 --> 21:31.190
Stop!

21:34.980 --> 21:35.940
Kaname-kun!

21:36.270 --> 21:37.820
Fumika, stop it!

21:38.280 --> 21:39.780
I wasn't going to shoot him.

21:39.780 --> 21:42.240
I was just trying to make him remember.

21:42.240 --> 21:44.370
Fumika, give me authorisation! Hurry!

21:51.210 --> 21:53.920
Fumika!

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Shigofumi

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Episode Seven

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Kirameki

23:27.340 --> 23:29.140
Time begins to move.

23:29.680 --> 23:31.180
At the boundaries of emotion...

23:31.180 --> 23:33.520
people notice the feelings of others.

23:35.020 --> 23:36.770
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:37.560 --> 23:38.690
The Beginning.

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Shigofumi

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Episode Eight

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
The Beginning
